AB  - Stateless broadcasting protocols in IoT networks are vulnerable to payload-level bit-flipping attacks. We present two attack schemes: physical-layer corruption detected by CRC and network-layer corruption that bypasses CRC. Using a LoRa mesh testbed, we show how a compromised node silently propagates false data, revealing critical vulnerabilities and motivating lightweight integrity defenses.  © 2025 IEEE.
