AB  - The proceedings contain 59 papers. The special focus in this conference is on AAL, Sensors Networks, Smart Cities and Security. The topics include: Probability and common-sense; ensemble learning-based algorithms for aggressive and agitated behavior recognition; motorized multi-camera slider for precise monitoring of physical rehabilitation; ambient displays to assist caregivers monitoring the sleep of people with dementia; physiological data acquisition system based on mobile computing; recognition of activities in resource constrained environments; reducing the computational complexity; activity recognition using dynamic instance activation; fall detection through thermal vision sensing; impact of medical history on technology adoption in Utah population database; improving the quality of user generated data sets for activity recognition; personalizing physical effort estimation in workplaces using a wearable heart rate sensor; ZigBee home automation localization system; enhancing smart environments with mobile robots; reliable publish/subscribe in dynamic ubiquitous systems; scheduling real-time traffic in underwater acoustic wireless sensor networks; a network performance analysis of LoRa modulation for LPWAN sensor devices; fine-tuning the DARP wireless sensor routing protocol; lightweight multivariate sensing in WSNs; WSN related requirement analysis towards sustainable building automation operations and maintenance; leader-based routing in mobile wireless sensor networks; self-organizing connectivity for mobile agents in dynamical environments; benchmarking Bluetooth SPP communications for ubiquitous computing; a rapid deployment solution prototype for IoT devices; using beacons for creating comprehensive virtual profiles; robot-based video surveillance application and a comparative study between RTSP and WebRTC.
