AB  - The proceedings contain 55 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Embedded Wireless Systems and Networks. The topics include: X-Lab: A Federated Testbed Infrastructure to Benchmark Geographically-Distributed Low-Power Wireless Systems; IPv6 over Bluetooth Advertisements: An alternative approach to IP over BLE; feasibility of Communication Between Sensor Nodes On-board Spacecraft Using Multi Layer Insulation; BISON: Attacking Bluetooth’s Broadcast Isochronous Streams; hardening and Speeding Up Zero-interaction Pairing and Authentication; AIRISC-A mmWave Angle-Insensitive Reconfigurable Intelligent Surface Communication System; A Game-Theoretic Approach for Mitigating Jamming Attacks in LPWAN; supporting the Adaptive Deployment of Modular Applications in Cloud-Edge-Mobile Systems; QualityBLE: A QoS Aware Implementation for BLE Mesh Networks; black carbon proxy sensor model for air quality IoT monitoring networks; InSight: Enabling NLOS Classification, Error Correction, anAnchor Selection on Resource-Constrained UWB Devices; Recovering Headerless Frames in LR-FHSS; demos: Robust Orchestration for Autonomous Networking; revisiting Cellular Throughput Prediction over the Edge: Collaborative Multi-device, Multi-network in-situ Learning; Demo: Video over Synchronous Flooding with OSFv6; demo: Sensor Node Communication Through Conductive Mesh Placed on Cotton Knit Fabric; demo: Audio Streaming Via Body-Coupled Communication; Demo: Hijacking Bluetooth’s Broadcast Audio Streams using BISON; OSA evaluation by using clinical parameters monitoring system based on Radar Technology; Poster: Towards a Flexbile Network API for Fat In-body Communication; poster: Resource-Efficient Deep Subnetworks for Dynamic Resource Constraints on IoT Devices; poster: A Battery-free Backscatter Communication System for Non-persistent Carriers; poster Abstract: Anchor Placement Optimization for Area-Based Localization Using Tabu Search Algorithm; poster: IoT-Edge-Cloud Continuum da