AB  - The sharp rise in urban traffic congestion has substantially delayed emergency medical response, often resulting in adverse patient outcomes and higher mortality rates. Recent studies underscore the need for intelligent ambulance routing systems capable of automatically prioritizing emergency vehicles through smart traffic management platforms. This paper proposes an integrated solution utilizing LoRa/DSRC-based communication for green corridor formation, Internet-of-Things (IoT)-driven traffic signal pre-emption, and real-time ambulance tracking, referencing established work by Schooler et al., Sutar et al., and others. The proposed architecture fuses GPS-enabled vehicle tracking, predictive analytics for route optimization, and AI-based dashboards for hospital coordination, while comparing the strengths of wireless protocols (LoRa, DSRC, ZigBee) in terms of latency, reliability, and deployment flexibility. Pilot deployments indicate that these systems can reduce ambulance travel time by up to 40%, with improved golden-hour survival rates and lower incident congestion. Experimental results validate the interoperability, security, and cost-effectiveness of such solutions across smart city infrastructures. Future work is motivated by the need for scalable AI frameworks, seamless integration with hospital EMR systems, and universal standardization of V2X protocols for emergency response networks, advancing beyond current state-of-the-art implementations. © 2025 IEEE.
