AD  - Dalian Polytechnic University, School of Information Science and Engineering, Dalian, China
AB  - The traditional fixed water quality detection system faces the problems of low coverage and the inability to obtain the full picture of water quality in the whole watershed in real time. In this paper, we designed a detection system based on LoRa and 4G communication technology, which consists of a collection terminal and a gateway. The collection terminal took an STM32 microcontroller, integrated a power management circuit, PH detection circuit, turbidity detection circuit, water temperature detection circuit, and TDS detection module to design the water quality monitoring node, and utilized LoRa networking technology to realize the uploading of monitoring data to the gateway. The gateway completed the data upload management of collection terminals, summarized the data from multiple collection terminals, added fixed headers to construct transmission messages, and transmitted the data to the server through 4G wireless technology. To meet the requirements of high coverage deployment of collection terminals, we analyzed and selected a mesh and star hybrid network topology, designed LoRa networking protocols, realized automatic management of the network topology, and at the same time, put forward network auto-configuration and channel quality verification for the link disconnection caused by various obstacles in the process of LoRa communication. Through the test, the system's packet loss rate was found to be less than 5%, the average data transmission time was 3.9 s, and the error rate for each acquisition parameter was less than 10%, which met the experimental design requirements. © 2024 IEEE.
