AB  - The proceedings contain 51 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Internet of Things, Communication and Intelligent Technology. The topics include: Design of Helmet Wearing Detection System Based on Cloud Edge Collaboration Technology; a Novel Multi-attention Convolutional Method for Human Activity Recognition; Research on 0.46 THz Ultra-High Order Harmonic Gyrotron Based on Axis-Encircling Electron Beam; Joint Beamforming and Trajectory Design for UAV-Assisted Power Grid Inspection with Integrated Sensing and Communication; an Efficient Routing Algorithm for Sea Buoy Network; Securing VANETs with Decentralized Certificate Management: A Tangle-Based Approach; a Dynamic Negative Sampling-Based Unsupervised Contrastive Learning for Hyperspectral Anomaly Detection; research and Application of Network Remote Operation Security Based on Sqlite Database; Compact Universal UHF Printed Dipole Antenna for Handheld RFID Readers; massive Internet of Things Terminal Security Control Technology Based on Malicious Behavior Multiple Network Traces Detection Association; research on Attack Path Prediction of Cyber-Physical Systems in Power Generation Side Based on Weighted Colored Petri Net; Rehabilitation Action Recognition Based on Deep Learning: A Hybrid Model Combining SE-ResBlock3D and LSTM; an Automatic Assignment Model for Power Operation and Maintenance Work Orders Based on Fit Degree; theoretical Proposal of a High Efficiency and Broadband Polarization Conversion Metasurface; iospheric Storm Monitoring and Positioning Method Based on Dual-Frequency Combination; Intelligent Agricultural Greenhouse Data Acquisition and Transmission and Equipment Control System Based on IOT; quantum Key Distribution Mechanism for Smart Grids; design and Implementation of Soil Monitoring System Based on LoRa; an Intelligent Logic Simulation System Method of Embedded Device.
