TY  - CONF
AU  - Gonzalo Andrés, J.
AU  - Román Gallego, J.Á.
TI  - Development and Deployment of a Secure, Decentralized Communication Prototype for Emergencies Using Interconnected LoRa Radio Nodes
PY  - 2026
T2  - Proceedings of 2026 5th International Conference on Cyber Security, Artificial Intelligence and Digital Economy, CSAIDE 2026
SP  - 85
EP  - 90
DO  - 10.1145/3819836.3819848
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105050625701?origin=resultslist
AD  - Air Institute, Zamora, Spain
AD  - University of Salamanca, Zamora, Spain
AB  - A reliable, independent, wide-range, and low-energy communication solution has been notably lacking for widespread adoption by key community sectors - such as volunteer teams, law enforcement, and emergency services - during high-impact emergency situations. Current centralized infrastructures have proven critically vulnerable, as evidenced by the 2024 DANA in Valencia, where the collapse of mobile networks and the Internet left entire populations isolated. To address this fragility, this work presents the development of a decentralized communication prototype based on LoRa radio technology and ESP32 microcontrollers. The system implements a mesh network topology that allows nodes to autonomously retransmit messages, extending the reach without external base stations. Security is ensured through ChaCha20-Poly1305 end-to-end encryption, complemented by a decentralized key management system using QR codes for secure physical exchanges. A multi-platform interface was developed using Flutter, ensuring a user-friendly experience for coordination. Field tests in real urban environments validated the proposed architecture, achieving a point-to-point range of at least 500 meters without intermediate nodes or external infrastructure. It is concluded that the featured system represents a viable, secure, and independent solution for critical messaging, ensuring operational communication even during the total failure of traditional networks.  © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
